# GitHub reads this file from the repository root, from `docs/`, or from
# `.github/`; it stays at the root deliberately, where a reader browsing
# the repository sees it next to MAINTAINERS.md. The workspace does have a
# `.github/` directory now — `.github/workflows/ci.yml` runs the four
# checks, the MSRV build, and the trademark checker — and the website
# still deploys separately, from the `er7-rust.github.io` repository this
# one's site subdirectory is split into.
#
# One line, one owner, no exceptions: this project has a single maintainer,
# and MAINTAINERS.md says so plainly rather than implying a team. When a
# second maintainer joins, this file gains a line for the areas they own,
# and MAINTAINERS.md gains a row, in the same change.
#
# An email address is used rather than a GitHub handle deliberately: it is
# the identity that owns the crates.io publishes and the commit history,
# and it does not change if a username does. GitHub only auto-requests a
# review from an email owner when that address belongs to a user with
# access to the repository, which is the case here.

